{"id":"e87d41c0c4a10896934d1b0aca87c712484ae6e3","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"e87d41c0c4a10896934d1b0aca87c712484ae6e3","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/serving/online_serving/token_in_token_out.md","lines":["@@ -191,6 +191,61 @@ With `return_token_ids`, the response carries `mm_hashes` next to `mm_placeholde"," - The processor cache is disabled (`--mm-processor-cache-gb 0`), so the returned keys can't be reused."," - The server runs the Rust frontend (`VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1`) which doesn't support omitting `kwargs_data` yet. It still returns `mm_hashes`."," ","+### Processed tensors in object storage","+","+A client that already has an item's processed tensors, such as an RL trainer on another node, can upload them to an S3-compatible store and send a reference in `features.kwargs_refs` instead of inlining them in `kwargs_data`. The tensors then skip the request body and any gateway in front of vLLM. The server downloads each object, checks its size and SHA-256 digest, and rebuilds the model's field metadata before it submits the request to the engine.","+","+Each object holds one item, saved with `safetensors.torch.save`. Its tensors are the ones this server's multimodal processor produces for that item, under the same names and dtypes and with their batch dimension, so the same tensors that `/render` returns in `kwargs_data`. The client doesn't need vLLM, but the tensors can differ from what the model's Hugging Face processor returns. For example, Qwen3-VL with the default `mm_device_do_normalize` normalizes on the GPU, so its object holds a `uint8` `pixel_values` and an `image_grid_thw` of shape `[1, 3]`:","+","+```python","+import hashlib","+","+import boto3","+from safetensors.torch import save","+","+payload = save({\"pixel_values\": pixel_values, \"image_grid_thw\": image_grid_thw})","+key = f\"rollouts/{request_id}/image-0\"","+boto3.client(\"s3\").put_object(Bucket=\"mm-tensors\", Key=key, Body=payload)","+","+features = {","+    \"mm_hashes\": {\"image\": [image_hash]},","+    \"mm_placeholders\": {\"image\": [{\"offset\": 15, \"length\": 64}]},","+    \"kwargs_refs\": {","+        \"image\": [{","+            \"uri\": f\"s3://mm-tensors/{key}\",","+            \"format\": \"safetensors-v1\",","+            \"nbytes\": len(payload),","+            \"digest\": hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest(),","+        }]","+    },","+}","+```","+","+Like `kwargs_data`, each `kwargs_refs` list is parallel to `mm_hashes`, and a `null` entry falls back to `kwargs_data` or the processor cache. An item can't set both. `mm_metadata` for a referenced item may only repeat fields of its object with the same values. The `mm_hashes` entry stays the cache key, so give different content different hashes.","+","+`kwargs_refs` are off by default. Enable them at startup with `--mm-tensor-refs-config`; a server started without it rejects them with a 400:","+","+```bash","+vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct --enable-scale-out \\","+    --mm-tensor-refs-config '{\"s3_allowed_uri_prefix\": \"s3://mm-tensors/rollouts\"}'","+```","+","+The config's fields are:","+","+- `s3_allowed_uri_prefix`: the `s3://bucket/prefix` that every reference must be under. Required.","+- `max_object_bytes`: the largest object the server downloads. Default: 1 GiB.","+- `max_request_bytes`: the largest total size of the objects one request references. A request over it fails with a 400 before anything is downloaded. Default: 1 GiB.","+- `max_reserved_bytes`: the memory one API server reserves for referenced tensors. Each request reserves twice the declared size of its objects, for the downloaded bytes and the decoded tensors, and keeps the reservation until it finishes, even if the client disconnects. Requests wait in arrival order until their reservation fits. It must be at least twice `max_request_bytes`. Default: 8 GiB.","+- `max_concurrent_reads`: how many requests per API server can download references at once. Default: 32.","+","+The endpoint and credentials come from the server's environment, never from the request: `S3_ENDPOINT_URL` if set, otherwise the standard boto3 configuration (for example `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3`, or `addressing_style` in the AWS config file). The server needs `boto3` installed, creates its S3 client at startup, and never deletes objects, so expire them on the client side, for example with a bucket lifecycle rule. Only the Python frontend accepts `kwargs_refs`.","+","+Like `kwargs_data`, `kwargs_refs` is meant for clients in one trust domain:","+","+- The server reads objects with its own credentials, so every caller of the endpoint can reference every object the server can read under the allowed prefix. Don't share a prefix between callers that shouldn't see each other's objects.","+- A missing, inaccessible or mismatched object (wrong size or digest) returns the same 422, so a caller can't probe objects it doesn't know. The details are in the server log.","+- The server checks each object's size, digest and fields, but tensors with a shape the model doesn't expect, such as `pixel_values` rows of the wrong width, can still fail inside the engine.","+"," ## Aborting requests"," "," `POST /inference/v1/abort_requests` aborts in-flight requests. It is registered wherever `/inference/v1/generate` is and requires the API key when `--api-key` is set, like `/inference/v1/generate`."],"additions":55,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/src/cmd/src/cli/unsupported.rs","lines":["@@ -420,6 +420,12 @@ pub struct ServerUnsupportedArgs {","     #[arg(long, env = \"VLLM_MAX_TOKENIZE_TOKENS\")]","     pub max_tokenize_tokens: Option<Unsupported>,"," ","+    /// Enable `features.kwargs_refs` in `/inference/v1/generate`, which loads","+    /// processed multimodal tensors that clients upload to an S3-compatible","+    /// store.","+    #[arg(long)]","+    pub mm_tensor_refs_config: Option<Unsupported>,","+","     /// Enable offline FastAPI documentation for air-gapped environments.","     /// Uses vendored static assets bundled with vLLM.","     ///"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/common/test_cli_args.py","lines":["@@ -247,6 +247,30 @@ def test_rust_grpc_port_requires_serve_subcommand(monkeypatch):","         validate_parsed_serve_args(args)"," "," ","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    (\"extra_args\", \"ok\"),","+    [","+        ([\"--no-enable-scale-out\"], False),","+        ([\"--enable-scale-out\"], True),","+        ([\"--no-enable-scale-out\", \"--tokens-only\"], True),","+    ],","+)","+def test_mm_tensor_refs_config_requires_generate_endpoint(serve_parser, extra_args, ok):","+    \"\"\"The config only does anything where /inference/v1/generate is served.\"\"\"","+    args = serve_parser.parse_args(","+        [","+            \"--mm-tensor-refs-config\",","+            '{\"s3_allowed_uri_prefix\": \"s3://bucket/prefix\"}',","+            *extra_args,","+        ]","+    )","+    if ok:","+        validate_parsed_serve_args(args)","+    else:","+        with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"--mm-tensor-refs-config requires\"):","+            validate_parsed_serve_args(args)","+","+"," def test_enable_auto_choice_fails_without_tool_call_parser(serve_parser):","     \"\"\"Ensure validation fails if tool choice is enabled with no call parser.\"\"\"","     # If we enable-auto-tool-choice, explode with no tool-call-parser"],"additions":24,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/scale_out/render/test_render.py","lines":["@@ -175,7 +175,9 @@ async def render_chat(request, raw_request=None, **kwargs):","         openai_serving_models=MagicMock(),","         tool_server=None,","     )","-    init_scale_out_state(state, MagicMock(), MagicMock(), None)","+    init_scale_out_state(","+        state, MagicMock(mm_tensor_refs_config=None), MagicMock(), None","+    )","     # Exercise conversion through both handlers without sampling or generation.","     state.serving_render.render_chat_request = renderer.render_chat","     fields = dict("],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/scale_out/token_in_token_out/test_generate_stream.py","lines":["@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@"," from unittest.mock import AsyncMock, MagicMock, patch"," "," import pytest","+import torch"," "," from vllm.config.multimodal import MultiModalConfig"," from vllm.entrypoints.generate.base.protocol import DeltaMessage, StreamOptions","@@ -363,6 +364,43 @@ async def test_serve_tokens_rejects_invalid_shm_handle_before_engine_handoff():","     engine.generate.assert_not_called()"," "," ","+@pytest.mark.asyncio","+async def test_null_kwargs_refs_fall_back_to_inline_data():","+    \"\"\"`null` references don't need the feature enabled or a read slot.\"\"\"","+    engine = _mock_engine()","+","+    async def mock_generate(*args, **kwargs):","+        yield _make_request_output(","+            \"req-1\", token_ids=[10], finish_reason=\"stop\", finished=True","+        )","+","+    engine.generate = MagicMock(side_effect=mock_generate)","+    serving = _build_serving_tokens(engine)","+    item = MultiModalKwargsItem(","+        {","+            \"pixel_values\": MultiModalFieldElem(","+                data=torch.zeros(1, 4), field=MultiModalBatchedField()","+            )","+        }","+    )","+    request = GenerateRequest(","+        token_ids=[1, 2, 3],","+        sampling_params=SamplingParams(max_tokens=1),","+        model=MODEL_NAME,","+        features=MultiModalFeatures(","+            mm_hashes={\"image\": [\"image_A\"]},","+            mm_placeholders={\"image\": [PlaceholderRangeInfo(offset=0, length=1)]},","+            kwargs_data={\"image\": [encode_mm_kwargs_item(item)]},","+            kwargs_refs={\"image\": [None]},","+        ),","+    )","+","+    response = await serving.serve_tokens(request)","+","+    assert isinstance(response, GenerateTokensResponse)","+    engine.generate.assert_called_once()","+","+"," @pytest.mark.asyncio"," async def test_stream_basic():","     \"\"\"Streaming returns SSE chunks with correct token_ids and ends with [DONE].\"\"\""],"additions":38,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/scale_out/token_in_token_out/test_mm_serde.py","lines":["@@ -445,6 +445,81 @@ def test_kwargs_and_metadata_generate_does_not_require_ec():","     assert torch.equal(item[\"image_grid_thw\"].data, image_grid_thw.data)"," "," ","+def _referenced_item_features(metadata: dict | None) -> MultiModalFeatures:","+    return MultiModalFeatures.model_validate(","+        {","+            \"mm_hashes\": {\"image\": [\"ref\", \"cached\"]},","+            \"mm_placeholders\": {","+                \"image\": [{\"offset\": 0, \"length\": 1}, {\"offset\": 2, \"length\": 1}]","+            },","+            \"kwargs_refs\": {","+                \"image\": [","+                    {","+                        \"uri\": \"s3://tensor-bucket/tenant/request/image-0\",","+                        \"format\": \"safetensors-v1\",","+                        \"nbytes\": 1024,","+                        \"digest\": \"a\" * 64,","+                    },","+                    None,","+                ]","+            },","+            \"mm_metadata\": None","+            if metadata is None","+            else {","+                \"image\": [encode_mm_kwargs_item(MultiModalKwargsItem(metadata)), None]","+            },","+        }","+    )","+","+","+def test_tensor_reference_loads_item_and_accepts_matching_metadata():","+    _, pixel_values, image_grid_thw = _image_engine_input()","+    loaded: list[tuple[str, str]] = []","+","+    def load(modality, ref):","+        loaded.append((modality, ref.uri))","+        return MultiModalKwargsItem(","+            {\"pixel_values\": pixel_values, \"image_grid_thw\": image_grid_thw}","+        )","+","+    features = _referenced_item_features({\"image_grid_thw\": image_grid_thw})","+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"reference loader\"):","+        mm_kwargs_from_features(features)","+    item, cached = mm_kwargs_from_features(features, reference_loader=load)[\"image\"]","+","+    assert loaded == [(\"image\", \"s3://tensor-bucket/tenant/request/image-0\")]","+    assert cached is None","+    assert item is not None","+    assert set(item) == {\"pixel_values\", \"image_grid_thw\"}","+    assert item[\"pixel_values\"] is pixel_values","+    assert torch.equal(item[\"image_grid_thw\"].data, image_grid_thw.data)","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"change\", [\"value\", \"extra_field\"])","+def test_metadata_cannot_change_a_referenced_item(change):","+    \"\"\"Validated fields of a referenced item can't be overridden by metadata.\"\"\"","+    _, pixel_values, image_grid_thw = _image_engine_input()","+    if change == \"value\":","+        metadata = {","+            \"image_grid_thw\": MultiModalFieldElem(","+                data=image_grid_thw.data * 2, field=image_grid_thw.field","+            )","+        }","+    else:","+        metadata = {\"image_grid_thw\": image_grid_thw}","+","+    def load(modality, ref):","+        item = {\"pixel_values\": pixel_values}","+        if change == \"value\":","+            item[\"image_grid_thw\"] = image_grid_thw","+        return MultiModalKwargsItem(item)","+","+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"doesn't match its kwargs_refs object\"):","+        mm_kwargs_from_features(","+            _referenced_item_features(metadata), reference_loader=load","+        )","+","+"," def test_cache_hit_null_kwargs_keeps_metadata_slot():","     pixel_values = MultiModalFieldElem(","         data=torch.randn(5, 3, dtype=torch.float32),","@@ -533,3 +608,25 @@ def test_placeholder_roundtrip(is_embed):"," def test_placeholder_rejects_mismatched_is_embed():","     with pytest.raises(ValidationError, match=\"is_embed\"):","         PlaceholderRangeInfo(offset=0, length=4, is_embed=[True])","+","+","+def test_metadata_cannot_change_field_settings_of_a_referenced_item():","+    \"\"\"Equal data with another field config keeps the loaded item's config.\"\"\"","+    _, pixel_values, image_grid_thw = _image_engine_input()","+    assert image_grid_thw.field.keep_on_cpu","+    gpu_grid = MultiModalFieldElem(","+        data=image_grid_thw.data, field=MultiModalBatchedField(keep_on_cpu=False)","+    )","+","+    def load(modality, ref):","+        return MultiModalKwargsItem(","+            {\"pixel_values\": pixel_values, \"image_grid_thw\": image_grid_thw}","+        )","+","+    item, _ = mm_kwargs_from_features(","+        _referenced_item_features({\"image_grid_thw\": gpu_grid}),","+        reference_loader=load,","+    )[\"image\"]","+","+    assert item is not None","+    assert item[\"image_grid_thw\"].field.keep_on_cpu"],"additions":97,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/scale_out/token_in_token_out/test_protocol.py","lines":["@@ -177,6 +177,63 @@ def test_multimodal_features_reject_overlapping_placeholders(placeholders):","         _features(placeholders)"," "," ","+def _s3_ref(**overrides) -> dict:","+    return {","+        \"uri\": \"s3://tensor-bucket/tenant/request/image-0\",","+        \"format\": \"safetensors-v1\",","+        \"nbytes\": 1024,","+        \"digest\": \"a\" * 64,","+        **overrides,","+    }","+","+","+def test_tensor_reference_with_metadata_does_not_require_ec():","+    request = GenerateRequest.model_validate(","+        {","+            **_base_payload(),","+            \"features\": {","+                \"mm_hashes\": {\"image\": [\"a\"]},","+                \"mm_placeholders\": {\"image\": [{\"offset\": 0, \"length\": 1}]},","+                \"kwargs_refs\": {\"image\": [_s3_ref()]},","+                \"mm_metadata\": {\"image\": [\"encoded-metadata\"]},","+            },","+        }","+    )","+","+    assert request.features is not None","+    assert request.features.kwargs_refs is not None","+    (reference,) = request.features.kwargs_refs[\"image\"]","+    assert reference is not None","+    assert reference.uri == \"s3://tensor-bucket/tenant/request/image-0\"","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    (\"features\", \"match\"),","+    [","+        ({\"kwargs_refs\": {\"video\": [_s3_ref()]}}, \"same modalities\"),","+        ({\"kwargs_refs\": {\"image\": [_s3_ref(), None]}}, \"same length\"),","+        (","+            {\"kwargs_refs\": {\"image\": [_s3_ref()]}, \"kwargs_data\": {\"image\": [\"x\"]}},","+            \"both kwargs_data and kwargs_refs\",","+        ),","+        ({\"kwargs_refs\": {\"image\": [_s3_ref(backend=\"s3\")]}}, \"backend\"),","+        ({\"kwargs_refs\": {\"image\": [_s3_ref(format=\"pickle\")]}}, \"format\"),","+        ({\"kwargs_refs\": {\"image\": [_s3_ref(nbytes=0)]}}, \"nbytes\"),","+        ({\"kwargs_refs\": {\"image\": [_s3_ref(digest=\"abc\")]}}, \"digest\"),","+        ({\"kwargs_refs\": {\"image\": [_s3_ref(endpoint=\"http://x\")]}}, \"endpoint\"),","+    ],","+)","+def test_multimodal_features_reject_invalid_tensor_references(features, match):","+    with pytest.raises(ValidationError, match=match):","+        MultiModalFeatures.model_validate(","+            {","+                \"mm_hashes\": {\"image\": [\"a\"]},","+                \"mm_placeholders\": {\"image\": [{\"offset\": 0, \"length\": 1}]},","+                **features,","+            }","+        )","+","+"," def test_generate_request_rejects_placeholder_outside_prompt():","     with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"within the token_ids sequence\"):","         GenerateRequest("],"additions":57,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/scale_out/token_in_token_out/test_serving_multimodal_tokens.py","lines":["@@ -9,18 +9,39 @@"," tests (e.g. entrypoints/rl/weight_transfer/test_offline.py) deadlock-free."," \"\"\""," ","+import asyncio","+import hashlib","+import json","+import threading","+import uuid","+from dataclasses import replace","+from http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer","+"," import httpx"," import pytest"," import pytest_asyncio","+import torch"," from PIL import Image","+from safetensors.torch import save as save_safetensors"," "," from tests.utils import RemoteOpenAIServer","+from vllm.entrypoints.scale_out.token_in_token_out.mm_serde import (","+    decode_mm_kwargs_item,","+    encode_mm_kwargs_item,","+)","+from vllm.multimodal.inputs import MultiModalBatchedField, MultiModalKwargsItem"," from vllm.multimodal.utils import encode_image_url"," "," MODEL_NAME = \"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct\""," GEN_ENDPOINT = \"/inference/v1/generate\""," RENDER_ENDPOINT = \"/v1/chat/completions/render\""," DETOKENIZE_ENDPOINT = \"/detokenize\"","+S3_BUCKET = \"mm-tensors\"","+S3_PREFIX = \"rollouts\"","+# GETs of keys under `concurrent/` wait until this many are in flight.","+CONCURRENT_READS = threading.Barrier(2, timeout=30)","+# Keys of every GET the store served.","+GET_PATHS: list[str] = []"," "," "," @pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")","@@ -29,7 +50,39 @@ def test_image():"," "," "," @pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")","-def server():","+def s3_store():","+    \"\"\"Objects served by a local stand-in for an S3 endpoint, by `bucket/key`.\"\"\"","+    objects: dict[str, bytes] = {}","+","+    class Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):","+        def do_GET(self):","+            path = self.path.removeprefix(\"/\")","+            GET_PATHS.append(path)","+            if \"/concurrent/\" in path:","+                CONCURRENT_READS.wait()","+            body = objects.get(path)","+            self.send_response(404 if body is None else 200)","+            body = body or b\"<Error><Code>NoSuchKey</Code></Error>\"","+            self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))","+            self.end_headers()","+            self.wfile.write(body)","+","+        def log_message(self, *args):","+            pass","+","+    httpd = ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", 0), Handler)","+    thread = threading.Thread(target=httpd.serve_forever, daemon=True)","+    thread.start()","+    try:","+        yield f\"http://127.0.0.1:{httpd.server_port}\", objects","+    finally:","+        httpd.shutdown()","+        httpd.server_close()","+        thread.join()","+","+","+@pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")","+def server(s3_store):","     args = [","         \"--dtype\",","         \"bfloat16\",","@@ -38,9 +91,25 @@ def server():","         \"--enforce-eager\",","         \"--no-enable-prefix-caching\",","         \"--enable-scale-out\",","+        \"--mm-tensor-refs-config\",","+        json.dumps(","+            {","+                \"s3_allowed_uri_prefix\": f\"s3://{S3_BUCKET}/{S3_PREFIX}\",","+                # Room for about three 224x224 items, so a leaked","+                # reservation blocks later requests.","+                \"max_request_bytes\": 1024**2,","+                \"max_reserved_bytes\": 2 * 1024**2,","+            }","+        ),","     ]","+    env = {","+        \"S3_ENDPOINT_URL\": s3_store[0],","+        \"AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\": \"test\",","+        \"AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\": \"test\",","+        \"AWS_DEFAULT_REGION\": \"us-east-1\",","+    }"," ","-    with RemoteOpenAIServer(MODEL_NAME, args) as remote_server:","+    with RemoteOpenAIServer(MODEL_NAME, args, env_dict=env) as remote_server:","         yield remote_server"," "," ","@@ -342,3 +411,241 @@ async def test_content_parts_streaming(client, test_image):","     first = prompt_metadata_chunks[0]","     assert first[\"mm_hashes\"] == render_data[\"features\"][\"mm_hashes\"]","     assert all(\"mm_hashes\" not in c for c in chunks if c is not first)","+","+","+def _upload_processed_image(","+    s3_store, render_data: dict, key_dir: str = \"\", **extra_tensors","+) -> dict:","+    \"\"\"Store the rendered item's tensors with their batch dimension.","+","+    Returns its `kwargs_refs` entry.","+    \"\"\"","+    _, objects = s3_store","+    item = decode_mm_kwargs_item(render_data[\"features\"][\"kwargs_data\"][\"image\"][0])","+    tensors = {","+        name: elem.data[None]","+        if isinstance(elem.field, MultiModalBatchedField)","+        else elem.data","+        for name, elem in item.items()","+    }","+    # A `None` value drops that tensor.","+    tensors = {k: v for k, v in {**tensors, **extra_tensors}.items() if v is not None}","+    payload = save_safetensors(tensors)","+    key = f\"{S3_PREFIX}/{key_dir}{uuid.uuid4().hex}/image-0\"","+    objects[f\"{S3_BUCKET}/{key}\"] = payload","+    return {","+        \"uri\": f\"s3://{S3_BUCKET}/{key}\",","+        \"format\": \"safetensors-v1\",","+        \"nbytes\": len(payload),","+        \"digest\": hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest(),","+    }","+","+","+@pytest.mark.asyncio","+async def test_kwargs_refs_generate_like_inline_kwargs_data(","+    client, s3_store, test_image","+):","+    \"\"\"Tensors loaded from S3 must generate the same tokens as inline ones.","+","+    The referenced item gets a new `mm_hash` so the encoder runs on the","+    loaded tensors instead of reusing the inline request's output. The","+    requests run one at a time, so greedy outputs are comparable.","+    \"\"\"","+    render_data = await _render_image_prompt(","+        client, encode_image_url(test_image, format=\"PNG\")","+    )","+    features = render_data[\"features\"]","+    reference = _upload_processed_image(s3_store, render_data)","+","+    outputs = []","+    for request_features in (","+        features,","+        {","+            \"mm_hashes\": {\"image\": [f\"ref-{uuid.uuid4().hex}\"]},","+            \"mm_placeholders\": features[\"mm_placeholders\"],","+            \"kwargs_refs\": {\"image\": [reference]},","+        },","+    ):","+        gen_resp = await client.post(","+            GEN_ENDPOINT,","+            json={","+                \"token_ids\": render_data[\"token_ids\"],","+                \"features\": request_features,","+                \"sampling_params\": {\"max_tokens\": 10, \"temperature\": 0.0},","+            },","+        )","+        gen_resp.raise_for_status()","+        outputs.append(gen_resp.json()[\"choices\"][0][\"token_ids\"])","+","+    assert outputs[0]","+    assert outputs[1] == outputs[0]","+","+","+@pytest.mark.asyncio","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    (\"change\", \"status\", \"error\"),","+    [","+        (\"uri\", 400, \"configured prefix\"),","+        (\"request_size\", 400, \"in one request declare\"),","+        (\"missing\", 422, \"Could not load multimodal tensor object\"),","+        (\"conflicting_metadata\", 400, \"doesn't match its kwargs_refs object\"),","+        (\"extra_tensor\", 422, \"not compatible with the served model\"),","+        (\"zero_dim\", 422, \"not compatible with the served model\"),","+        (\"short_rows\", 422, \"not compatible with the served model\"),","+        (\"extra_rows\", 422, \"not compatible with the served model\"),","+        (\"negative_grid\", 422, \"not compatible with the served model\"),","+        (\"grid_only\", 422, \"not compatible with the served model\"),","+    ],","+)","+async def test_invalid_kwargs_refs_are_rejected(","+    client, s3_store, test_image, change, status, error","+):","+    \"\"\"Bad references fail with a client error and leave the server healthy.\"\"\"","+    render_data = await _render_image_prompt(","+        client, encode_image_url(test_image, format=\"PNG\")","+    )","+    item = decode_mm_kwargs_item(render_data[\"features\"][\"kwargs_data\"][\"image\"][0])","+    pixel_values = item[\"pixel_values\"].data","+    grid = item[\"image_grid_thw\"].data[None]","+    extra = {","+        \"extra_tensor\": {\"attention_mask\": torch.ones(1, 4)},","+        \"zero_dim\": {","+            \"pixel_values\": torch.tensor(1, dtype=torch.uint8),","+            \"image_grid_thw\": torch.tensor([[1, 2, 2]]),","+        },","+        # Fewer or more patches than image_grid_thw describes.","+        \"short_rows\": {\"pixel_values\": pixel_values[:-4]},","+        \"extra_rows\": {\"pixel_values\": torch.cat([pixel_values, pixel_values[:4]])},","+        # A negative size would slice from the end and still yield enough rows.","+        \"negative_grid\": {","+            \"pixel_values\": torch.cat([pixel_values, pixel_values]),","+            \"image_grid_thw\": grid * torch.tensor([1, -1, 1]),","+        },","+        # Only the grid, nothing for the vision encoder.","+        \"grid_only\": {\"pixel_values\": None},","+    }.get(change, {})","+    reference = _upload_processed_image(s3_store, render_data, **extra)","+    if change == \"uri\":","+        reference[\"uri\"] = reference[\"uri\"].replace(S3_PREFIX, \"other\", 1)","+    elif change == \"request_size\":","+        reference[\"nbytes\"] = 1024**2 + 1","+    elif change == \"missing\":","+        s3_store[1].clear()","+","+    features = render_data[\"features\"]","+    request_features = {","+        \"mm_hashes\": features[\"mm_hashes\"],","+        \"mm_placeholders\": features[\"mm_placeholders\"],","+        \"kwargs_refs\": {\"image\": [reference]},","+    }","+    if change == \"conflicting_metadata\":","+        # A stale grid in mm_metadata would undo the row-count check.","+        grid_elem = item[\"image_grid_thw\"]","+        stale = replace(grid_elem, data=grid_elem.data * torch.tensor([1, 2, 1]))","+        request_features[\"mm_metadata\"] = {","+            \"image\": [","+                encode_mm_kwargs_item(MultiModalKwargsItem({\"image_grid_thw\": stale}))","+            ]","+        }","+    gen_resp = await client.post(","+        GEN_ENDPOINT,","+        json={","+            \"token_ids\": render_data[\"token_ids\"],","+            \"features\": request_features,","+            \"sampling_params\": {\"max_tokens\": 1},","+        },","+    )","+","+    assert gen_resp.status_code == status","+    assert error in gen_resp.text","+    assert (await client.get(\"/health\")).status_code == 200","+","+","+@pytest.mark.asyncio","+async def test_kwargs_refs_are_read_concurrently(client, s3_store, test_image):","+    \"\"\"Two requests must be able to read their references at the same time.","+","+    Each GET blocks until the other one arrives, so serialized reads time out.","+    \"\"\"","+    render_data = await _render_image_prompt(","+        client, encode_image_url(test_image, format=\"PNG\")","+    )","+    features = render_data[\"features\"]","+","+    async def generate():","+        reference = _upload_processed_image(s3_store, render_data, \"concurrent/\")","+        return await client.post(","+            GEN_ENDPOINT,","+            json={","+                \"token_ids\": render_data[\"token_ids\"],","+                \"features\": {","+                    \"mm_hashes\": {\"image\": [f\"ref-{uuid.uuid4().hex}\"]},","+                    \"mm_placeholders\": features[\"mm_placeholders\"],","+                    \"kwargs_refs\": {\"image\": [reference]},","+                },","+                \"sampling_params\": {\"max_tokens\": 1},","+            },","+        )","+","+    for gen_resp in await asyncio.gather(generate(), generate()):","+        gen_resp.raise_for_status()","+","+","+@pytest.mark.asyncio","+async def test_kwargs_refs_release_their_memory(client, s3_store, test_image):","+    \"\"\"Each request returns its reservation, streamed or not.","+","+    The server's budget fits about three of these items, so a request that","+    kept its reservation would make a later one wait forever.","+    \"\"\"","+    render_data = await _render_image_prompt(","+        client, encode_image_url(test_image, format=\"PNG\")","+    )","+    features = render_data[\"features\"]","+    async with asyncio.timeout(120):","+        for stream in [False, True] * 4:","+            body = {","+                \"token_ids\": render_data[\"token_ids\"],","+                \"features\": {","+                    \"mm_hashes\": {\"image\": [f\"ref-{uuid.uuid4().hex}\"]},","+                    \"mm_placeholders\": features[\"mm_placeholders\"],","+                    \"kwargs_refs\": {","+                        \"image\": [_upload_processed_image(s3_store, render_data)]","+                    },","+                },","+                \"sampling_params\": {\"max_tokens\": 2},","+                \"stream\": stream,","+            }","+            async with client.stream(\"POST\", GEN_ENDPOINT, json=body) as resp:","+                assert resp.status_code == 200","+                text = \"\".join([chunk async for chunk in resp.aiter_text()])","+            assert \"token_ids\" in text","+","+","+@pytest.mark.asyncio","+async def test_bad_reference_is_rejected_before_any_download(","+    client, s3_store, test_image","+):","+    \"\"\"A disallowed reference fails the request before the valid one is read.\"\"\"","+    data_url = encode_image_url(test_image, format=\"PNG\")","+    render_data = await _render_image_prompt(client, data_url, data_url)","+    valid = _upload_processed_image(s3_store, render_data)","+    outside = {**valid, \"uri\": valid[\"uri\"].replace(S3_PREFIX, \"other\", 1)}","+    features = render_data[\"features\"]","+","+    gen_resp = await client.post(","+        GEN_ENDPOINT,","+        json={","+            \"token_ids\": render_data[\"token_ids\"],","+            \"features\": {","+                \"mm_hashes\": features[\"mm_hashes\"],","+                \"mm_placeholders\": features[\"mm_placeholders\"],","+                \"kwargs_refs\": {\"image\": [valid, outside]},","+            },","+            \"sampling_params\": {\"max_tokens\": 1},","+        },","+    )","+","+    assert gen_resp.status_code == 400","+    assert \"configured prefix\" in gen_resp.text","+    assert valid[\"uri\"].removeprefix(\"s3://\") not in GET_PATHS"],"additions":309,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/multimodal/test_tensor_transport.py","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,378 @@","+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project","+\"\"\"Tests fo